{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f2c87b41-63e0-517b-b97c-4f90b53275da",
    "name": "Consent Manager \u2014 Data Fiduciary API",
    "description": "The API a data fiduciary's systems call: raise consent requests one at a time or by the thousand, read where each\nstands, verify a consent token before using personal data, and read the fiduciary's own billing and audit trail.\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery call except the public keys needs one of:\n\n- **An API key** in `X-API-Key` (`cmk_\u2026`), issued in the DF Console under *Developers \u2192 API keys* (ADR-041).\n- **An OAuth 2.0 access token** from client credentials (`df-api-<your fiduciary id>`), in `Authorization: Bearer`.\n\nNever send both.\n\n## Signed requests (replay protection)\n\nEach API key comes with a signing secret (`cms_\u2026`). A signed request carries three more headers:\n\n| Header | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `X-Signature-Timestamp` | The current time in Unix seconds |\n| `X-Signature-Nonce` | A new random value for **every** request: 16\u201364 of `A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -` |\n| `X-Signature` | Lower-case hex HMAC-SHA256 of the text below, keyed by the signing secret's UTF-8 bytes |\n\nThe signed text is these seven lines joined by `\\n`, with no trailing newline:\n\n```text\nCM1-HMAC-SHA256\n{X-Signature-Timestamp}\n{X-Signature-Nonce}\n{HTTP method, upper case}\n{path exactly as sent, without the query}\n{query string exactly as sent, without '?', or empty}\n{lower-case hex SHA-256 of the exact body bytes (of no bytes when there is no body)}\n```\n\n- The timestamp must be within **\u00b1300 seconds** of the server's clock (`signature-expired` otherwise).\n- A nonce is accepted **once** per key: the same signed request sent again is refused with **409\n  `request-replayed`**. Retries are signed afresh with a new nonce.\n- A key can **require** signatures: then every unsigned `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH` or `DELETE` is refused\n  (`signature-required`). Reads may go unsigned. A request carrying any signature header is always checked.\n- Multipart uploads are signed like any other body: hash the exact bytes you send.\n\n## Errors\n\nErrors are `application/problem+json` (RFC 9457) with a stable `title`, such as `quota-exceeded` or\n`request-replayed`.\n\n## Environments\n\nUse the **sandbox** to integrate: the same API, its own keys and data, test contacts only (`*@sandbox.example`,\n`+44 7700 900000`\u2013`900999`), nothing delivered.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// CM1-HMAC-SHA256 (ADR-041): sign the method, path, query and exact body with a fresh timestamp and nonce.",
          "const cryptojs = require('crypto-js');",
          "const secret = pm.variables.get('signingSecret');",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-API-Key', value: pm.variables.replaceIn('{{apiKey}}') });",
          "if (!secret || pm.request.body && pm.request.body.mode === 'formdata') {",
          "  // no secret, or a multipart upload Postman builds after this script: sent unsigned",
          "  ['X-Signature', 'X-Signature-Timestamp', 'X-Signature-Nonce'].forEach(h => pm.request.headers.remove(h));",
          "  return;",
          "}",
          "const offset = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('timestampOffset') || 0); // the replay demo backdates one request",
          "const timestamp = (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) + offset).toString();",
          "const fixed = pm.collectionVariables.get('fixedNonce'); // the replay demo reuses one nonce",
          "const nonce = fixed || (cryptojs.lib.WordArray.random(16).toString(cryptojs.enc.Hex));",
          "const method = pm.request.method.toUpperCase();",
          "const path = '/' + pm.request.url.path.map(p => pm.variables.replaceIn(p)).join('/');",
          "const query = pm.request.url.query.filter(q => !q.disabled)",
          "  .map(q => q.key + (q.value === null || q.value === undefined ? '' : '=' + pm.variables.replaceIn(q.value))).join('&');",
          "const body = pm.request.body && pm.request.body.mode === 'raw' ? pm.variables.replaceIn(pm.request.body.raw) : '';",
          "if (pm.request.body && pm.request.body.mode === 'raw') {",
          "  pm.request.body.update(body); // send exactly the bytes signed",
          "}",
          "const canonical = ['CM1-HMAC-SHA256', timestamp, nonce, method, path, query, cryptojs.SHA256(body).toString(cryptojs.enc.Hex)].join('\\n');",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-Signature-Timestamp', value: timestamp });",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-Signature-Nonce', value: nonce });",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-Signature', value: cryptojs.HmacSHA256(canonical, secret).toString(cryptojs.enc.Hex) });"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
